      "source_mix": "Reuters-syndicated reporting, court reporting, and an official ministry notice. The evidentiary mix is strong for direct public rhetoric and mixed for family-finance allegations.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "Country priors are better than the low-score cases but still show substantial corruption and accountability weaknesses. They are used only as background because the chapter turns on Bolsonaro's own speech, appointments, and family-linked scrutiny.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Bolsonaro's 2022 integrity record is poor and repeatedly adversarial toward truth-tellers, but the dossier still stops short of a full extraction case. He publicly pushed unsupported electoral-fraud claims, attacked journalists, and faced family-finance scrutiny that gives the record a strong personal-nexus problem. At the same time, the file includes one professional appointment and one investigative conclusion that limits the strongest obstruction claim. That combination places him below a mixed or merely sloppy ruler, but above the clearest kleptocratic and systematically concealed cases.",
      "lower_anchor_rejected": "A score of 1 is too low because the dossier does not show a fully documented, centralized theft-and-concealment regime with direct adjudicated personal extraction.",
      "higher_anchor_rejected": "A score of 4 or higher would understate the repeated deception, hostility to scrutiny, and family-linked conflict concerns shown here.",
