      "source_mix": "OCCRP, HRW, Reuters, local media, and official reporting. The dossier is strong on inner-circle allegations and weaker on final adjudication of personal benefit.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "Country priors show very weak rule-of-law and corruption control. They are not treated as evidence of Tshisekedi's personal honesty, but they help explain why the dossier mixes correction and patronage so heavily.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Tshisekedi's integrity record is mixed and somewhat worse than a clean reformer, but it is not a pure extraction case. The strongest negatives are the adviser caught on tape negotiating a corrupt mineral deal and the patronage-heavy appointment pattern around public enterprises. The strongest positives are his office's anti-spoliation moves, anti-corruption institutional actions, and the formal Court of Accounts appointment. That combination supports a low-middling score rather than a sharply punitive one.",
