      "source_mix": "Official parliamentary record plus German media reporting on hearings and a court order. The record is relatively strong on institutional scrutiny and relatively weak on personal-benefit allegations.",
      "structured_prior_summary": "High accountability and strong rule-of-law priors provide a supportive baseline, but they are not used as proof of Scholz's personal integrity. The score reflects the actual scrutiny record around Cum-Ex.",
      "chapter_rationale": "Scholz is generally more defensible than a low-integrity ruler, but the dossier is not a full integrity slam-dunk. He testified under oath-like political scrutiny, faced a court order, and remained inside a functioning accountability environment. At the same time, the Cum-Ex record never becomes a clear, costly admission or a clean exoneration of the broader controversy. That is a solid but not exceptional integrity profile: mostly honest in office, materially opaque on a major earlier scandal, and better than a mixed or evasive ruler.",
